    "Hint.NextIntervalTiles": "Takes a note's tile count from the gap before it, the gap after it, or the shorter of the two.",
    "NextIntervalHelp": "Gap before: a note is as busy as the run it just came from. Gap after: as busy as what is coming. Both gaps: as busy as the shorter of the two, whichever side it is on. In 2K, when the gaps on both sides of a note add up to less than twice the 4K boundary (a lane would come back too soon), the count goes up on that note instead of waiting for the cycle to end.",
    "StateNextGap": "the gap after",
    "StatePreviousGap": "the gap before",
    "Chord keeps the lane before it": "Chord keeps the lane before it",
    "Hint.ChordAvoidBeforeLanes": "The single right before a chord keeps off the chord's lanes.",
    "ChordBeforeHelp": "Chords are placed after the singles, so the single is the one that moves: 3 3-4 becomes 2 3-4. It stays where it is when no lane is free.",
    "StateChordBeforeOn": "the single steps aside",
    "StateChordBeforeOff": "left as placed",
    "Restart the pattern each run": "Restart the pattern each run",
    "Hint.RestartPatternOnRun": "Starts the pattern again where the gaps close up.",
    "RunRestartHelp": "A note whose gap before it is more than 1.5 times the gap after it opens a run of three to eight notes (two is not a run, and a stream of more than eight is left alone), and the pattern starts from its first tile there, so a burst of three reads 4-3-2 / 4-3-2. It starts one tile later when the first would repeat the last one. A restart that would bring the lane just played back within twice the faster boundary is not made; the cycle carries on.",
    "StateRunRestartOn": "from the first tile",
    "StateRunRestartOff": "carries on",
    "Enhanced chord and trill rules": "Enhanced chord and trill rules",
    "Hint.EnhancedChordRules": "Keeps a chord in place where chords come back with one to three singles between them, and puts the singles beside it.",
    "EnhancedChordsHelp": "Where chords come back with one to three singles between them, the singles never move the chord: it keeps the first chord's lanes. One single reads 1-2 3, two 1-2 3 4, three 1-2 3 4 3, and three faster than the 4K boundary alternate with 1-2 4 3 4. Four or more stay as they were, except that four going back and forth on two lanes right before a chord (1 2 1 2 3-4) are laid out another way when one fits.",
